      "h1": "Redemptionist EVR (aka RED EVR",
      "excerpt": "Redemptionist EVR (aka RED EVR &ndash; Leqtiqueshop Skip to content Submit Close search Leqtiqueshop Submit Search Log in Cart Redemptionist EVR (aka RED EVR Regular price $210.00 Sale Default Title - Sold out Quantity Sold out RED EVR Gallery In 2009, when I was officially starting my career as Shun Nokina Design, I designed the \"Redemptionist,\" commonly known as \"RED.\" The design was inspired by the intensely smooth and dynamic sounds of Brett Garsed and, at one point, Allan Holdsworth. The treble was kept under control, maintaining a smooth sound at all points, with only a slight change in the flavor of the high-mids. The gain ranged from clean to high gain to suit all Jazz, Fusion, and Shred genres. The low cut was controlled so that it would not affect the texture of the distortion at any point, and so that the \"audibility\" could be adjusted to suit the playing environment. That was the concept. (09' SND Redemptionist: Since then I have been fascinated by Scandinavia, so the motif is the flags of the Scandinavian peninsula. 15 years later, EVR was realized based on my experience of living in various Scandinavian countries.) In 2014, the Leqtique brand released the RED, with a major overhaul of the circuitry and a redesign to accommodate a wider range of music. Compared to the original SND RED, it lost some of its intense smoothness, but it expanded the treble range as much as possible while still achieving a sensual tone. As a result, it was the most versatile pedal in the Leqtique lineup, and is suitable for a wide range of genres, including pop and rock. During the five years it was manufactured and sold, it was the brand's best-selling overdrive/distortion pedal, second only to the MAT and 9/9. Now, the design of the 2025 Redemptionist EVR (aka RED EVR) began with the idea of \u200b\u200bfirst cloning the Leqtique RED in EVR format, then adding something extra. In a modern music scene that focuses more on high frequencies, the idea of \u200b\u200badding something extra just to the treble control was something that crossed my mind during the design process. To be honest, the balance of the Leqtique RED was already at a point where it was impossible to tweak any further, so this was quite a difficult problem. In the end, after tweaking various points in the circuit, I brought in only the filtering ideas (ratios) used in the SND Red. Although the sound itself is completely unrelated, I managed to maintain a smooth tone while slightly raising the treble range and center of gravity. My design concepts often aim to create products that specialize in a particular genre, but the RED EVR is extremely versatile, and it allows you to experience the common EVR format, so it's a great choice as your first EVR pedal. Or, for hardcore users, I hope you'll enjoy this ongoing part of the 15-year-old Red lineage. Shun Nokina About the \"EVR\" concept Since 2019, I have been based in Europe and have been involved in the design of several pedals, but the Leqtique pedal line has essentially been on hiatus without releasing any new products. However, by temporarily moving my base to Iceland in 2024, I was able to gain some wonderful inspiration, and have continued to design all of them as an updated package called \"EVR.\" \"EVR\" is the Icelandic word for Europe. The letters strongly evoke the idea that the pedals embody the inspiration and experiences gained over many years of traveling and living in various parts of Europe. The Leqtique pedals originally embodied a strong desire for Europe, with their vibrant paintwork and dark sound, but now they are more clearly embodied as a more real-world experience. Leqtique pedals, which have not received an update in 15 years, have been completely redesigned from the ground up, including the housing, all components, and concept. For example, the housing, which was previously a one-piece machined aluminum body, has been redesigned from a standard \"box\" design with a wide tolerance range, but has been completely redesigned ",
